export anchor TopNavHubStyle:
    number: 175
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Top nav hub
    idea: A classic hub page with a navy bar of horizontal navigation and sub-tabs on top, a full-width stone band of four large figures, and three equal ruled columns for projects, the chart and activity, on warm grey paper.
    base: light
    palette:
        navy: #1d2c54, the top bar, headings, figures, panel top rules, the primary button, this week bars and focus
        navyInk: #c9d1e6, nav links that are not current on navy
        page: #f3f1ed, the warm grey page
        paper: #ffffff, panels, the sub-tab bar, fields and the style sheet
        band: #e8e4dc, the full-width figures band and initials squares
        ink: #25262b, body text and project names
        muted: #5e5a53, labels, notes, meta and day numbers
        line: #d9d4cb, panel borders and row rules
        strongLine: #858077, dividers inside the figures band, field borders and last week bar outlines
        ok: #2d6a3e, On track text and check circle
        risk: #8a4d00, At risk text and triangle
        bad: #a8261e, Behind and overdue text, crossed square and clock
    type:
        One humanist stack, Avenir Next, Avenir, Segoe UI, Helvetica Neue,
        Helvetica, Arial. Base 15px at 1.5. Band figures are 44px at 600
        with tabular numbers, the greeting 30px bold navy, panel titles and
        band labels 12 to 13px bold caps tracked 0.1em, project names 15px
        bold, meta 13px.
    layout:
        Stacked full-width bands inside a 1232px container. A navy top bar
        holds a square outline mark and the Brightwork wordmark, the six nav
        items as horizontal tabs with a white underline on Home, then a
        white search field, a white New project button, an outlined bell and
        Mara Okafor at right. A white sub-tab bar beneath holds Overview, My
        tasks, Timeline and Workload with a navy underline on Overview, and
        the date with a calendar icon at right. The greeting sits on the
        page with the overdue line and a Review them link. A full-width
        stone band runs edge to edge with four figures split by vertical
        rules, each a caps label, a 44px navy number and a short note,
        overdue in red with a clock. Then three equal columns of white
        panels with a 3px navy top rule. Projects lists six rows of name,
        status, category and due, and a 6px bar. The chart panel shows
        fourteen bars, hatched outlined last week and solid navy this week,
        over a small table of week totals and change. Activity lists six
        entries with square initials. Below 1040px the nav wraps under the
        brand and activity spans two columns. Below 760px the nav becomes a
        three by two grid, figures go two by two and panels stack.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px gutters between columns, 20px figure padding, 12 to 18px row padding, 28px above the columns.
    density: Medium. Figures are large and airy, the columns beneath are compact.
    corners: Nearly square. 3px panels, buttons and fields, round avatar, square initials.
    borders: 1px warm grey panel borders and row rules, a 3px navy top rule on panels, darker vertical rules in the band.
    shadows: None. Hierarchy comes from the navy bar, the stone band and rules.
    icons:
        Line icons at 2px stroke, 18px. Status is text with a check circle
        for On track, a triangle for At risk, a crossed square for Behind
        and a clock for overdue.
    focus: A 3px navy outline offset 2px with a white gap, white and inset on the navy bar.
    tone: Formal and businesslike, with caps labels such as Due this week and Hours logged and plain links such as All projects.
